  "body": "Stacked on #3993 (which is stacked on #3992 and #3990). This branch starts from `issue/1120-ground-inks`. Its own commit is the last one (a165c5cfe). Review that commit only. Merge #3990, #3992 and #3993 first.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe third family of #1120: the viewport overlay inks. With it, the viewport family of #1120 is done.\n\n- Ten colour tokens join `Tokens`. Each is also a theme-file key (`colors.<name>`):\n  - the generate progress panel: `overlay_panel`, `overlay_edge`, `overlay_text`, `overlay_track`;\n  - the file drop hint: `drop_veil` (its frame and text read `overlay_text`);\n  - the empty 3D view: `empty_hint`;\n  - the dark halo under a picked edge and under the Geometry-list row hover: `pick_halo`;\n  - the fixture plate marks: `plate_hole`, `plate_dowel`;\n  - the move of the selected G-code line: `gcode_line`.\n- Both tables hold the old values, so no pixel changes. These draw sites did not follow the viewport ground, so the ground rule of #3993 does not apply to them: a key that a file omits keeps its base value.\n- The outline of the origin triads (`shell.rs`, black at alpha 170) reads the existing `handle_shade`: the same value and the same role. Its user-guide row now names the triads.\n- `pick_ink.rs` reads `pick_halo` too. `HALO_ALPHA` stays; the test pins the token against it.\n- Draw sites: `gen_overlay.rs`, `file_drop.rs`, `shell.rs`, `pick_ink.rs`. `shell.rs` has CRLF line ends; the commit keeps them.\n- The colour-literal guard loses the rows of `gen_overlay.rs`, `file_drop.rs` and `shell.rs`. `theme/tables.rs` goes from 62 to 82.\n- The example theme and the colour table of the user guide have the ten keys.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/1120-overlay-inks.md`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\nIn `crates/ui/tests/theme_files/viewport_inks.rs`, a module of the existing `theme_files` test binary (#3187: no new binary):\n\n- `the_built_in_columns_keep_the_overlay_colours`: both tables carry the old literals, `pick_halo` equals `from_black_alpha(HALO_ALPHA)`, and `handle_shade` is the old triad outline.\n- `each_overlay_ink_is_a_theme_key`: each key sets its own ink, and a file that changes the viewport ground does not change the overlays.\n\nAlso: `theme_example::example_loads_and_holds_the_dark_defaults` and `theme_files::colour_literals::no_colour_literal_outside_the_allowed_rows`.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nThe generate panel (a job that runs), the file drop hint over the demo Block (the origin triads are under it), and the empty 3D view, in the dark and light theme. The images come from the off-screen renderer (`egui_kittest` with the headless wgpu device, as in `guide_images`), at 1280 x 720. The images are on the images-only `pr-screenshots` branch of the fork, not on this branch.\n\nA pixel comparison of each pair gives 0 different pixels, with one exception. In the generate panel, 14 (dark) and 62 (light) pixels differ, all in a strip 4 pixels high: the activity bar, which sweeps with the clock.\n\n| | Before (eef05252f) | After (a165c5cfe) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Generate panel, dark | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/1120-overlays/before-gen-panel-dark.png) | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/1120-overlays/after-gen-panel-dark.png) |\n| Generate panel, light | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/1120-overlays/before-gen-panel-light.png) | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/1120-overlays/after-gen-panel-light.png) |\n| Drop hint, dark | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/1120-overlays/before-drop-hint-dark.png) | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/1120-overlays/after-drop-hint-dark.png) |\n| Drop hint, light | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/1120-overlays/before-drop-hint-light.png) | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/1120-overlays/after-drop-hint-light.png) |\n| Empty view, dark | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/1120-overlays/before-empty-view-dark.png) | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/1120-overlays/after-empty-view-dark.png) |\n| Empty view, light | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/1120-overlays/before-empty-view-light.png) | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/1120-overlays/after-empty-view-light.png) |\n\nThe images do not show the fixture plate marks, the selected G-code move, or the pick halo. The tests pin those values.\n\n## Gates\n\nOn the head a165c5cfe:\n\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`): 10 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (2.6 min). It includes `ui suites: lib`, `ui suites: theme_example` and `ui suites: theme_files` (30 tests).\n- `cargo clippy --no-deps --all-targets -p camcraft-ui -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Heavy lanes: the diff reaches none.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No check by hand in the GUI. The tests and the pixel comparison pin the values.\n\nChangelog: Themes can set the generate progress panel, the file drop hint, the empty-view text, the pick halo, the fixture plate marks and the selected G-code move colours.\n\nRefs #1120\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
